import { TerminalCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> TerminalCopy = TerminalCopy {
  summary: "ProcessError describes why reading settings, arguments, a working directory, or other process information failed. InvalidEnvironmentName identifies an invalid setting name.",
  taskTitle: "Explain an empty or NUL-containing setting name",
  purpose: "Try reading a setting with an empty name and with a name containing a NUL character. Both produce InvalidEnvironmentName, allowing the same message to explain valid names. No real setting or secret value needs to be read.",
  typescriptBefore: "This TypeScript readSetting helper checks for an empty or NUL-containing name before accessing process.env. The validation is added deliberately to compare the same input policy as Seseragi; native process.env access in Node.js or Bun does not necessarily produce the same error.",
  benefit: "Match the process.InvalidEnvironmentName shape instead of comparing error text. Keep a branch for other failures so that only a name problem receives the specific guidance about valid names.",
  reading: [
    "inspectName is an effect fn that accepts a String argument named name and tries to read that setting. main passes an empty string, then \"BAD\\0NAME\". Inside a string, \\0 represents the NUL control character, not the digit 0.",
    "Left (process.InvalidEnvironmentName _) matches just the invalid-name failure. The _ ignores the name carried by the error. Left reason handles other failures, and Right _ handles a successful read.",
    "Both calls print Use a nonempty setting name without a NUL character. In main, _ <- inspectName \"\" finishes the first operation before proceeding and ignores its return value."
  ],
  details: [
    "ProcessError has public error constructors such as process.InvalidEnvironmentName that you can match. The page’s opaque-type classification does not prevent using those public constructors to distinguish errors.",
    "Reading a valid name that does not exist succeeds with Nothing. That differs from a read failing because its name is invalid. Right _ here reports only that the name was accepted, regardless of whether a value exists.",
    "This example reproduces rejection of empty and NUL-containing names. Failures involving text conversion or access to the working directory cannot necessarily be reproduced with the same input on every OS.",
    "After handling ProcessError, the println that reports the outcome can still fail with ConsoleError. The main declaration’s fails ConsoleError describes that separate output failure."
  ]
}
